  "summary": "Claude Code runs project hooks/MCP before trust approval (CVE-2025-59536)",
  "details": "Check Point Research reported that malicious repository configuration (Hooks, MCP servers) could execute commands when an untrusted project is opened, before the user approves trust. NVD: versions before 1.0.111 vulnerable. A related issue, CVE-2026-21852, let a repo setting redirect API traffic (including the key) before the trust prompt; one source says versions before 2.0.65.",
